---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Second Edition — CMNA"
  description="A public staging area for corrections, updates, and second-edition-scale ideas around CMNA."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A second edition should have a reason to exist.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is where changes substantial enough to outgrow the 2017 text can
        accumulate in public.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="content">
        <div class="callout">
          <strong>No second edition is being announced here.</strong> The purpose of
          this section is to keep revision material organized so that a future
          edition, if undertaken, begins with evidence rather than vague intentions.
        </div>

        <h2>What can accumulate here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>verified errata and clarifications;</li>
          <li>modernized R idioms where the language or ecosystem has changed;</li>
          <li>better examples for methods that deserve more room;</li>
          <li>reproducible figures and computational demonstrations;</li>
          <li>teaching notes generated by actual classroom use; and</li>
          <li>new material that fits the book's scope rather than merely fitting the field.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The standard</h2>
        <p>
          New material should earn its way into a new edition. A changed package
          version is not, by itself, a reason to rewrite a book. A clearer treatment,
          a better computational example, a corrected weakness, or a genuinely useful
          addition is.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Corrections</h3>
          <p>
            The previous CMNA page records an errata update dated April 3, 2019.
            Detailed corrections will be migrated here once the source material is
            consolidated.
          </p>
          <a href="https://jameshoward.us/books/computational-methods-numerical-analysis-r/">Existing book page →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card aside-card">
          <h3>Development signal</h3>
          <p>
            The companion software provides a concrete place to see what has been
            maintained, corrected, tested, or extended since publication.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/k3jph/cmna-pkg">Package repository →</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
